{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"Implementation detail for this story (exact line-level edit list for kept files and tests; the description carries the decisions). Line numbers are on origin/main 2e81cb9767c1.\n\nEdit (kept src): `src/rebar/_store/event_append.py:385-387` (comment + call) and `:423-430` (`_maybe_enrich_drain`); `src/rebar/_store/push.py:590-596` (drain block at the tail of `push_after_commit`); `src/rebar/llm/plan_review/attest.py:216-233` (whole try/except; `return sig` at `:234` stays; the `logging` import stays, `:46` uses it); `src/rebar/llm/plan_review/__init__.py:600-612`; `src/rebar/_engine_support/reads_cli.py:186-188` (comment), `:190-201` (keep `out = dict(state)` at `:194`); `src/rebar/_cli/_llm_commands.py:548-561`; `src/rebar/_cli/_registry.py:427,453` (reword `:444`); `src/rebar/_cli/__init__.py:65-70`; `src/rebar/llm/__init__.py:44,113`; `src/rebar/llm/config.py:47,55` (re-exports), `:114-143` (13 `DEFAULT_OVERLAP_*` + comments), `:408-426` (13 fields), `:505,521` (this story owns only these lines; the config epic owns every other line in this file); `src/rebar/llm/config_readers.py:133-138` (`_llm_drain_mode`), `:211-317` (`_read_llm_overlap_settings`); `src/rebar/llm/config_binding.py:55-67` (13 allowlist names); `src/rebar/llm/contracts.py:150-249` (`ticket_digest_response_model`, `overlap_verdict_response_model`, `overlap_verdict_batch_response_model`), `:290-297` (three `register_contract`s; keep `:298-299`), reword `:261`; `src/rebar/schemas/__init__.py:68,80` (`__all__`), `:147-155` (`TICKET_DIGEST`, `OVERLAP_VERDICT`), `:385-391` (`\"enrich\"`, `\"overlap_judge\"` entries); `src/rebar/_commands/doctor_locks.py:104,109,380-386` (drop the `enrich-drain` leg, otherwise a leftover `.rebar/enrich-drain.lock` with no producer is a permanent `stale` finding that doctor never clears, `_existence_report` `:271-281`), reword `:43-52` to five legs; `src/rebar/schemas/doctor.schema.json:47` enum entry and the two \"enrichment drain lock\" mentions in `:5`; `src/rebar/_config_schema.py:81-84` docstring becomes \"Warns at create time when another ticket with the same normalized title was created inside the recency window (rebar create duplicate_warning).\" (this story owns only these lines); `src/rebar/reducer/_version.py:43-57` and `src/rebar/_store/event_prepare.py:69-80` comments become \"Retired producer (ADR 0086, removed in granitic-realisable-dolphin); the name is kept so historical events still parse and compaction preserves them.\" with names and the `:133-134` error string unchanged; `rebar.toml:32-42` becomes a comment \"Create-time same-title duplicate journal (`rebar create` stderr / `duplicate_warning`); advisory only, never blocks a create. The store-wide overlap detector this key used to gate was removed (ADR 0086 retired).\" plus `suggest_duplicate_tickets = true`; delete `rebar.toml:205-216` (the `[llm]` header at `:204` stays); `scripts/probe_rebar.py:557` (drop the `digest_freshness` bullet), `:571` becomes `{\"inbound_deps\", \"plan_review_health\"}`.\n\nEdit (tests): `tests/unit/test_config_llm.py:126-142,146,153,168-180`; `tests/unit/test_env_registry_helper_coverage.py:34-36`; `tests/unit/test_push_callers_best_effort.py:23`; `tests/unit/test_plan_review_resign.py:64`; `tests/unit/test_llm_commands_render.py:67`; `tests/unit/test_detached_child_cwd.py:3-4,33,115,126,142,154` (drop the drain arm); `tests/unit/test_spawn_detached.py:107,119`; `tests/unit/store/test_stamped_lock.py:411,417-421,457,460`; `tests/unit/store/test_store_paths.py:59,106-107,232-249`; `tests/scripts/graph/test_doctor_locks.py:83,284,557` (five legs; retarget the two lock paths to `compact-worker.lock`); `tests/integration/test_concurrency_regression.py:2056-2131` (delete that test); `tests/scripts/test_llm_seam_clean_heldout.py:36,41`; `tests/interfaces/contracts/test_cli_help_writing_guidelines_jerboa.py:33,75,99`; `tests/interfaces/facades/test_intercept_registry_cutover_s6_heldout.py:77-79`; `tests/unit/test_cli_registry_cutover_s6.py:5`; `tests/unit/test_run_request_builder.py:132,139,152,173,191` (`output_schema=\"epic_bug_screen_verdict\"`); `tests/unit/test_subcall_class_selection.py:21-22,91,126-127`; `tests/unit/test_step_failures.py` (rename the `\"overlap-judge\"` literal to `\"epic-bug-screen\"` at `:33-35,52,61,74-75,124-129,290-296,319-325`); `tests/unit/test_schema_complexity_gate.py:215`; `tests/unit/test_store.py:185-186`.\n\nAdd test: in `tests/interfaces/contracts/test_event_schema_forward_compat.py`, `test_retired_overlap_event_types_still_parse`: seed a ticket, write one raw event file per name (mirror `_write_future_event` at `:66-78`; `data` from the shapes the deleted `test_ticket_digest_store.py` and queue tests used), assert each name is in `_NON_REPLAY_KNOWN_TYPES`, `is_unknown_newer_type(n) is False`, `n in event_append.EVENT_TYPES`, `rebar.show_ticket(tid)[\"status\"] == \"open\"` with `\"digest_freshness\" not in state`, `rebar compact` leaves the four files on disk, and `rebar.fsck(repo_root=...)` contains neither `\"newer than this rebar understands\"` nor `\"CORRUPT\"`.\n\nRegenerate: `python scripts/gen_cli_help.py && python scripts/gen_cli_reference.py && python scripts/gen_env_registry.py && python scripts/gen_config_reference.py && python -m rebar.llm.prompting.prompts regenerate-index && python scripts/gen_api_surface.py --update && python scripts/gen_mcp_reference.py` (touches `docs/cli-reference.md:838,1004-1018`, `docs/env-vars.md:69-81`, `docs/config-reference.md:69`, `src/rebar/_cli/help/overview.txt:53`, `tests/unit/api_surface_baseline.json`). Do not hand-edit `.github/complexity-baseline.json` (`:39` becomes `stale`, passes per `scripts/check_complexity_baseline.py:68-71`) or `.github/mechanism-baseline.json` (`:519-531,655` become `stale`, passes per `scripts/check_mechanism_delta.py:14,54`; `:86` and `:637` stay live). `tests/golden/config_surface.json` inventories `_config_schema._SECTIONS` only, so no regen.\n\nCross-epic ownership: the CLI-consolidation epic owns `_help_route._REMOVED_SPELLINGS`; this story appends one `\"enrich\"` entry to it (if this story lands first, the entry goes into the existing frozenset and the CLI epic migrates it). Whichever of the two lands second regenerates `help/overview.txt` and `docs/cli-reference.md` after rebase; never hand-merge them."},"env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1788805019370728307,"uuid":"9ba3382c-068d-4821-ac4d-becc21597dae"}